{
  "openapi": "3.2.1",
  "info": {
    "title": "IP2Location.io IP Geolocation API",
    "summary": "IP Geolocation",
    "description": "IP2Location.io IP Geolocation API returns location, network, mobile and security data for an IPv4 or IPv6 address in real time.\n\n**Plan-dependent fields.** The Free plan returns the 11 basic attributes. Starter adds ISP, domain, net speed, IDD and area codes, weather station, elevation and usage type. Plus adds translated place names, the continent, country, region, city, time zone and geotargeting objects, mobile data and address type. Security adds the full proxy object, the IP2Proxy fraud score, AS details and the advertising category. Every field is optional in the response schema because the set depends on the plan.\n\n**Authentication.** Send your API key as a Bearer token in the `Authorization` header (recommended), or as the `key` query parameter. Without a key, the IP geolocation endpoint allows 1,000 requests per day from the same client IP.\n\n**Rate limits.** Keyless requests are limited to 1,000 per day per client IP, reset at 00:00 UTC. A Free plan key allows up to 50,000 queries per month. Paid plans keep serving requests and bill overage.\n\nThe endpoint supports JSON and XML responses.",
    "version": "1",
    "termsOfService": "https://www.ip2location.io/terms-of-service",
    "contact": {
      "name": "IP2Location.io",
      "url": "https://www.ip2location.io",
      "email": "support@ip2location.io"
    },
    "license": {
      "name": "MIT",
      "url": "https://github.com/ip2location/ip2location-io-openapi/blob/main/LICENSE"
    }
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://api.ip2location.io",
      "description": "Global anycast endpoint."
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "IP Geolocation",
      "description": "Look up geolocation, network, mobile and proxy data for an IP address."
    }
  ],
